+<section class="material-notes section"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Material principles</p><div class="process-grid"><article><span class="drawing-number">01 / Keep</span><h3>Value what is there.</h3><p>Existing structures hold character and resources. We start by understanding their condition and capacity before proposing replacement.</p></article><article><span class="drawing-number">02 / Touch</span><h3>Choose for daily life.</h3><p>We favour tactile, repairable finishes that feel good in use. Samples are considered in the light and context of the room.</p></article><article><span class="drawing-number">03 / Time</span><h3>Allow things to age.</h3><p>Natural variation and honest wear give a place depth. We consider maintenance, adaptability and how details will change with use.</p></article></div></div></section>
