+<?php /** Practical questions in place of unverified client endorsements. */ ?>
+<section class="faq section container"><div><p class="eyebrow">Before we begin</p><h2>A few useful<br><em>questions.</em></h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Do I need a fully formed brief?</summary><p>No. A description of the place, what is difficult about it and what you hope to change is a useful beginning. We can help turn those thoughts into a brief with clear priorities.</p></details><details><summary>Can architecture and interiors be considered together?</summary><p>Yes. Thinking about room proportions, furniture, lighting and materials alongside the building plan helps the whole place feel coherent. The scope would be agreed at the start.</p></details><details><summary>How are fees and timing established?</summary><p>They depend on the site, complexity, required approvals and the level of support. A real engagement would begin with a written scope, stage-by-stage fees and an indicative programme. This sample site does not offer quotations.</p></details><details><summary>What if I want to work with an existing building?</summary><p>We begin by understanding its condition and history. Surveys and specialist advice may be needed before judging what can be retained, adapted or extended.</p></details></div></section>

